contractile function", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42290373"}, {"study_label": "Elamipretide animal RCT (preclinical)", "outcome": "single-fiber contractile function (soleus)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42290373"}, {"study_label": "Elamipretide animal RCT (preclinical)", "outcome": "muscle atrophy prevention", "arm": "mito", "direction": "positive", "significant": true, "evidence": "preclinical", "ref_id": "42290373"}, {"study_label": "PMD pharmacotherapies editorial (editorial)", "outcome": "sildenafil for Leigh syndrome (speculative)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "42229401"}, {"study_label": "Mito micronutrients (review)", "outcome": "clinical efficacy of micronutritional cocktails", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "meta", "ref_id": "42654282"}, {"study_label": "MNV-201 (Ph2)", "outcome": "safety / therapeutic effects (no results posted)", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT06017869"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "Elamipretide", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 5, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42794697", "40816230", "NCT05168774", "NCT05162768", "NCT07531251"]}, {"intervention": "Elamipretide", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42290373"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 3, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42361626", "42630618", "42650043"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["42495453", "42479041"]}, {"intervention": "MitoQ", "disease": "septic cardiomyopathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42460027"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted agents (class)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42440741"]}, {"intervention": "rAAV2/2-ND4 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42131170"]}, {"intervention": "LHON gene therapy (class reviews)", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42627399", "41318849"]}, {"intervention": "AAV2-ND6 allotopic gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42709484"]}, {"intervention": "NFS-02 gene therapy", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT05820152"]}, {"intervention": "NR082", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07406854"]}, {"intervention": "Idebenone (standard of care)", "disease": "Leber hereditary optic neuropathy", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42535808"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NR/NMN)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 3, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42669151", "42009009", "42489969"]}, {"intervention": "NMN", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42573891"]}, {"intervention": "Urolithin A", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42616901"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondria-targeted nanocarriers", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42022751"]}, {"intervention": "MNV-201 (placenta-derived mitochondria)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06017869"]}, {"intervention": "Mitochondrial-oriented micronutrition", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42654282"]}, {"intervention": "Restorin NR", "disease": "aging", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42582917"]}, {"intervention": "PMD pharmacotherapies (elamipretide/Kygevvi/sildenafil)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["42229401"]}], "insights": ["Chronic heart failure: a 2026 meta-analysis of mitochondria-targeted agents reports significant benefits vs control — LVEF (SMD 0.42; 95% CI 0.31–0.53), NYHA class (RR 2.38), all-cause mortality (RR 0.62), HF hospitalizations (RR 0.60) — but the comparator was control/placebo, not GDMT; no head-to-head mito-therapy vs GDMT trial exists, so advantage over standard of care is unproven (indirectness; low confidence for the SoC question). [42440741]", "LHON: allotopic rAAV2/2-ND4 gene therapy significantly improved BCVA (meta-analysis, n=175) but did NOT significantly increase responder rates; reviews add BCVA/retinal-sensitivity/QoL gains, and preclinical AAV2-ND6 restored visual function in mice without systemic toxicity. The standard-of-care idebenone meta-analysis shows only partial visual recovery with early treatment (not significant), and two late-stage gene-therapy trials (NFS-02 Ph1/2; NR082 Ph3, n=95) have no results posted — pipeline only. [42131170, 42627399, 42709484, 42535808, 41318849, NCT05820152, NCT07406854]", "Primary mitochondrial disease (elamipretide, Barth syndrome): accelerated approval for muscle-strength improvement exists, but cardiac disease modification remains unconfirmed; the strongest direct clinical evidence is a single n=1 case report with sustained improvement (low confidence), while the Ph3 RCT and the Ph4 RCT (n=48) have no posted results — evidence of pipeline activity only, not of effect. [42794697, 40816230, NCT05162768, NCT07531251]", "Negative/mixed signals are real: two meta-level reviews report early PMD antioxidant/metabolic trials as largely negative or mixed, with only four PMD therapies authorized to date; in the NR animal model, significant cardiac contractility benefit coexisted with significant WORSENING of erythrocyte maturation and anemia (bone-marrow reductive stress) — opposite directions across organs (inconsistency; low confidence); and in the NR+exercise RCT, peak VO2 improved vs control (p=0.03) but was null vs exercise alone, suggesting the gain may be exercise-driven. [42361626, 42630618, 42669151, 42009009]", "The PMD standard-of-care baseline is itself unproven: SoC is supportive cofactor/micronutrient therapy with no approved disease-modifying drug, and a 2026 review of those micronutritional interventions found disease-specific randomized evidence remains limited (efficacy unclear) — so 'mito vs standard' comparisons in PMD lack a validated active comparator. [42654282, 42229401]", "Preclinical depth far outpaces human confirmation: MitoQ (diabetic and septic cardiomyopathy), urolithin A, NMN, mito-targeted nanocarriers, and elamipretide in a mouse HF model consistently improved mitochondrial function, contractility, anti-fibrosis and anti-inflammation markers — all preclinical; only the class-level HF meta-analysis reaches human (aggregated) level, and no per-study human RCT for a single mito agent in GDMT-treated HF is represented in these records. [42290373, 42479041, 42460027, 42616901, 42573891, 42022751]"]}